course: dictionary
lesson: 1150
title: One word, many meanings: bright
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To pick the right one, read the words around it. The context shows which meaning the writer wants. «Where hands rub a brass door knob every day, the metal stays bright.» Here bright means shiny, because the knob is polished, not dull.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another sentence. «Tigers have bright white spots on the backs of their black ears.» Bright describes a strong colour that is easy to see. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence, and does my meaning still make sense when I swap it in?
explain: Bright can also describe a person or an idea. «She had a bright idea.» A bright idea is a clever one. Use the clues around the word, and check your choice by reading the whole sentence again.
fact: Bright has several meanings, so check the sentence to find the right one.
fact: «Bright» can mean giving out strong light, as in «a bright light».
fact: «Bright» can describe strong colours that are easy to see, as in «bright red».
fact: «Bright» can mean clever, as in «a bright pupil», or happy and lively, as in «a bright smile».
fact: Never look directly at the Sun, because it is very bright.
exercise: «Where hands rub a brass door knob every day, the metal stays bright.» What does bright mean here? | Loud and noisy | Heavy and cold | Shiny, not dull | *Shining, not dull
exercise: «Tigers have bright white spots on the backs of their black ears.» What does bright mean here? | Happy and lively | Late at night | Warm to touch | *Strong and easy to see
exercise: «Bright beach lights can lead hatchlings the wrong way.» Which meaning of bright fits? | Likely to be good | Happy and lively | *Giving out strong light | Clever and quick to learn
test: «She had a bright idea.» What does bright mean here? | Giving out light | Sad and tired | Strong colour | *Clever and good
test: «We set off bright and early.» What does bright and early mean? | Brightly lit by the Sun | Likely to be good | *Very early in the morning | Happy and lively
exam: «Her bright future as a scientist was certain.» What does bright mean in a bright future? | Giving out light | Clever and quick to learn | *Likely to be good | Strong colour
